back  on the cleveland browns he worked with  charlie frye learning the receiver  position  but you talk about you know how he was  helped on that team and here's what i'm  told  when he got there basically tom brady  when you get to the patriots you've been  drafted  by the patriots or you know you're  you're on the team  brady will basically start working with  you  until he senses that  you're not uh you're not working hard  and and and you're not going to be a guy  who  who i'm going to be able to rely on but  when that happened  with julian edelman that was the key to  him because tom brady  saw how hard this guy worked and he  would stay after and after and after  and you know and so those are the  reasons why guys succeed  in my opinion in new england you're  gonna get a chance  and as a receiver you're gonna get a  chance but  when the guy who basically is in charge  of determining  honestly whether you're gonna make it or  not if he sees  the desire the drive the work ethic he's  gonna beat you into the ground  to make it work with you same thing  happened when chris hogan went there  as a free agent so those are the kind of  things  that happened in new england now you  know we'll see what happens with the  tight ends this year  with cam newton and and how much  they're able to work together and a lot  of it too mike  is what are they going to be allowed to  do in this offseason  and i think that's going to be really  important in new england  those guys used to get together all the  time anyway  and now if they have organized workouts  or whatever it is  they're going to have to find a way to  get together this off season  we're going to be talking about that in  the next segment before we take our  break though you mentioned  julian edelman experimenting at the  nickel corner position  i still remember clearly him playing the  slot  against the ravens in a playoff game  once upon a time and  covering anquan bolden or more  accurately trying to  cover anquan bolton edelman picked the  right position ultimately to play other  than quarterback in the nfl because it  wasn't working  at defensive back even though he took 27  snaps out of 73 in that afc championship  game that the patriots ultimately won  over the ravens to cap the 2011 seas  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights  from nbc sports
 

